module

public import StacksFrontier.RingTheory.AutoAssociated

/-!
# Producing a weakly associated prime of a flat tensor product from its fibre

Let `R → S` be a ring map, let `N` be an `S`-module which is projective as an `R`-module and let
`M` be an `R`-module. Stacks 05IG characterises the primes of `S` weakly associated to `M ⊗_R N`
by two conditions on the prime `𝔭` of `R` below them: that `𝔭` be weakly associated to `M`, and
that the extension of the prime to the fibre ring `S ⊗_R κ(𝔭)` be associated to the fibre module
`N ⊗_R κ(𝔭)`. The implication from left to right is proved in
`StacksFrontier/RingTheory/Ideal/WeaklyAssociatedPrime/FlatTensorProduct.lean`. This file proves the
*converse* step, which is the last paragraph of the source's proof and the only place where its
auto-associated rings are used.

The situation of that paragraph is the one the earlier reductions of Stacks 05IG arrive at: `R` is
local with maximal ideal `𝔭`, the module `N` is projective over `R`, and the prime `𝔮` of `S` is
`𝔭S` together with finitely many further elements `g₁, …, gₙ`, which is what it means for its
extension to the fibre ring to be generated by `n` elements. The fibre condition enters in the
elementwise form it is used in: an element of `N` outside `𝔭N` which every element of `𝔮` carries
into `𝔭N`.

The conclusion produced here is a prime of `S` containing `𝔮`, lying over `𝔭`, and weakly
associated to `N ⊗[R] M`. In the source this prime is then shown to equal `𝔮` by the implication
already proved together with the maximality of the fibre prime among the associated primes of the
fibre module, which is the hypothesis the earlier reduction installs.

## Main results

* `Stacks.AutoAssociated.isAutoAssociated_quotient_of_radical_eq_maximalIdeal`: the quotient of a
  local ring by an ideal whose radical is the maximal ideal is auto-associated. This is the
  sentence "the local ring `R/I` is auto-associated as `𝔭/I` is locally nilpotent" of the source.
* `Stacks.AutoAssociated.not_injective_of_not_injective_rTensor`: over an auto-associated ring a
  map between projective modules which fails to be injective after some base change already fails
  to be injective. This is Stacks 05GP read contrapositively, with the base-changing module
  allowed to live in any universe.
* `Stacks.WeaklyAssociatedPrimes.exists_isWeaklyAssociatedPrime_tensorProduct_of_fibre`: the
  converse step of Stacks 05IG described above.

## Implementation notes

The module `N/IN` of the source, for `I` the annihilator of the chosen element of `M`, is realised
here as the base change `(R ⧸ I) ⊗[R] N`, which carries the `(R ⧸ I)`-module structure that the
auto-associated argument needs and is projective over `R ⧸ I` because `N` is projective over `R`.
The same module with the two factors exchanged, `N ⊗[R] (R ⧸ I)`, carries instead the `S`-module
structure that the annihilator of the element produced must be taken over, so the two appear side
by side and are compared by `TensorProduct.comm`; multiplication by an element of `S` on the
second corresponds on the first to the base change of multiplication on `N`.

Stacks 05GP is stated for modules in one universe, and the module it is base changed by in the
application — the residue field of the local ring — lives in the universe of the ring rather than
in that of `N`. `Stacks.AutoAssociated.not_injective_of_not_injective_rTensor` removes that
coupling by lifting the two projective modules and the base-changing module into a common
universe, so the statement of the converse step keeps independent universes for `R`, `S`, `N`
and `M`.

The fibre hypothesis is taken in the elementwise form rather than as membership in the associated
primes of the fibre module: only the existence of a nonzero element of the fibre annihilated by
the fibre prime is used, and taking it in that form keeps the statement free of the fibre ring and
makes it strictly more general than the source's.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 05IG](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/05IG)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 05GM](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/05GM)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 05GN](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/05GN)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 05GP](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/05GP)
-/

@[expose] public section

open scoped TensorProduct

universe u v w t

namespace Stacks.AutoAssociated

/-- **The quotient of a local ring by an ideal with maximal radical is auto-associated.**

If `I` is an ideal of a local ring `R` whose radical is the maximal ideal `𝔭`, then `R ⧸ I` is
local and its maximal ideal `𝔭/I` is its nilradical, hence the unique prime ideal of `R ⧸ I` and
in particular the unique minimal prime over the annihilator of `1`. So `𝔭/I` is weakly associated
to `R ⧸ I` as a module over itself.

This is the sentence "the local ring `R/I` is auto-associated as `𝔭/I` is locally nilpotent" in
the proof of Stacks 05IG. -/
theorem isAutoAssociated_quotient_of_radical_eq_maximalIdeal {R : Type u} [CommRing R]
    [IsLocalRing R] {I : Ideal R} (hI : I.radical = IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal R) :
    IsAutoAssociated (R ⧸ I) := by
  have hne : I ≠ ⊤ := by
    intro h
    refine (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal.isMaximal R).ne_top ?_
    rw [← hI, h, Ideal.radical_top]
  have : Nontrivial (R ⧸ I) := Submodule.Quotient.nontrivial_iff.mpr hne
  let hloc : IsLocalRing (R ⧸ I) :=
    IsLocalRing.of_surjective' (Ideal.Quotient.mk I) Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective
  have hann : ((R ⧸ I) ∙ (1 : R ⧸ I)).annihilator ≤ IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (R ⧸ I) := by
    intro b hb
    rw [Submodule.mem_annihilator_span_singleton, smul_eq_mul, mul_one] at hb
    simp [hb]
  refine ⟨hloc, 1, ⟨⟨(IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal.isMaximal (R ⧸ I)).isPrime, hann⟩, ?_⟩⟩
  intro J hJ _
  have hJp : J.IsPrime := hJ.1
  -- Every prime of `R ⧸ I` is the maximal ideal, because its preimage in `R` contains `I`,
  -- hence contains `I.radical = 𝔭`.
  have hcomap : I ≤ J.comap (Ideal.Quotient.mk I) := by
    intro a ha
    simp [Ideal.Quotient.eq_zero_iff_mem.mpr ha]
  have hle : IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal R ≤ J.comap (Ideal.Quotient.mk I) := by
    rw [← hI]
    exact (Ideal.radical_le_radical_iff.mpr (hcomap.trans Ideal.le_radical)).trans_eq
      (Ideal.IsPrime.radical (Ideal.comap_isPrime (Ideal.Quotient.mk I) J))
  intro x hx
  obtain ⟨a, rfl⟩ := Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective x
  refine hle ?_
  by_contra hamem
  exact IsLocalRing.notMem_maximalIdeal.mpr
    ((IsLocalRing.notMem_maximalIdeal.mp hamem).map (Ideal.Quotient.mk I)) hx

/-- **Stacks Project, Tag 05GP, contrapositively and across universes.** Over an auto-associated
ring, a map between projective modules which is not injective after base change along some module
is not injective.

Stacks 05GP says that over such a ring an injective map of projective modules is universally
injective, so it stays injective after every base change; the module base changed by is allowed
here to live in a universe of its own, which the formulation of universal injectivity does not
allow, by lifting all three modules into a common universe. -/
theorem not_injective_of_not_injective_rTensor {A : Type u} [CommRing A]
    (hA : IsAutoAssociated A) {P Q : Type v} [AddCommGroup P] [Module A P]
    [Module.Projective A P] [AddCommGroup Q] [Module A Q] [Module.Projective A Q]
    (f : P →ₗ[A] Q) {Z : Type w} [AddCommGroup Z] [Module A Z]
    (hZ : ¬ Function.Injective (f.rTensor Z)) : ¬ Function.Injective f := by
  intro hf
  refine hZ ?_
  let eP : ULift.{w, v} P ≃ₗ[A] P := ULift.moduleEquiv
  let eQ : ULift.{w, v} Q ≃ₗ[A] Q := ULift.moduleEquiv
  let eZ : ULift.{v, w} Z ≃ₗ[A] Z := ULift.moduleEquiv
  have : Module.Projective A (ULift.{w, v} P) := Module.Projective.of_equiv' eP.symm
  have : Module.Projective A (ULift.{w, v} Q) := Module.Projective.of_equiv' eQ.symm
  let f' : ULift.{w, v} P →ₗ[A] ULift.{w, v} Q := eQ.symm.toLinearMap ∘ₗ f ∘ₗ eP.toLinearMap
  have huni := (universallyInjective_iff_injective_of_projective
    (annihilator_ne_bot_of_isAutoAssociated hA) f').2
    (eQ.symm.injective.comp (hf.comp eP.injective)) (ULift.{v, w} Z)
  let eL : ULift.{w, v} P ⊗[A] ULift.{v, w} Z ≃ₗ[A] P ⊗[A] Z := TensorProduct.congr eP eZ
  let eR : ULift.{w, v} Q ⊗[A] ULift.{v, w} Z ≃ₗ[A] Q ⊗[A] Z := TensorProduct.congr eQ eZ
  have hsq : (f.rTensor Z).comp eL.toLinearMap
      = eR.toLinearMap.comp (f'.rTensor (ULift.{v, w} Z)) :=
    TensorProduct.ext' fun p z => by simp [eL, eR, f', eP, eQ, eZ]
  refine (Function.Injective.of_comp_iff' _ eL.bijective).1 ?_
  have : ⇑(f.rTensor Z) ∘ ⇑eL = ⇑eR ∘ ⇑(f'.rTensor (ULift.{v, w} Z)) :=
    congrArg DFunLike.coe hsq
  rw [this]
  exact eR.injective.comp huni

end Stacks.AutoAssociated

namespace Stacks.WeaklyAssociatedPrimes

variable {R : Type u} [CommRing R] {S : Type v} [CommRing S] [Algebra R S]
  {N : Type w} [AddCommGroup N] [Module S N] [Module R N] [IsScalarTower R S N]
  {M : Type t} [AddCommGroup M] [Module R M]

/-- The element of `S` obtained from an element of `R` whose image in the quotient `R ⧸ I`
annihilates `(R ⧸ I) ⊗[R] N` annihilates `N ⊗[R] (R ⧸ I)` as well. -/
private theorem smul_eq_zero_of_mem (I : Ideal R) {a : R} (ha : a ∈ I)
    (x : N ⊗[R] (R ⧸ I)) : (algebraMap R S a) • x = 0 := by
  have hR : a • x = 0 := by
    induction x with
    | zero => simp
    | tmul n b =>
        obtain ⟨b, rfl⟩ := Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective b
        rw [TensorProduct.smul_tmul' a n _, TensorProduct.smul_tmul,
          show a • Ideal.Quotient.mk I b = 0 by
            rw [Algebra.smul_def, Ideal.Quotient.algebraMap_eq, ← map_mul,
              Ideal.Quotient.eq_zero_iff_mem]
            exact I.mul_mem_right b ha,
          TensorProduct.tmul_zero]
    | add x y hx hy => rw [smul_add, hx, hy, add_zero]
  rw [← hR, algebraMap_smul]

/-- **The converse step of Stacks Project, Tag 05IG.**

Let `R` be a local ring with maximal ideal `𝔭`, let `R → S` be a ring map, let `N` be an
`S`-module which is projective as an `R`-module and let `M` be an `R`-module. Assume

* `𝔭` is weakly associated to `M`;
* the prime `𝔮` of `S` is `𝔭S + g₁S + ⋯ + gₙS` for finitely many `gᵢ`;
* some `z : N` outside `𝔭N` is carried into `𝔭N` by every `gᵢ`.

Then some prime of `S` containing `𝔮`, lying over `𝔭`, is weakly associated to `N ⊗[R] M`.

The last two hypotheses are the content of "the extension of `𝔮` to the fibre ring
`S ⊗_R κ(𝔭)` is generated by `n` elements and is associated to the fibre module `N ⊗_R κ(𝔭)`",
written out elementwise: the fibre ring is `S/𝔭S` and the fibre module is `N/𝔭N`.

The proof is the last paragraph of the source. Choose `y : M` whose annihilator `I` has radical
`𝔭`, which is possible because `R` is local and `𝔭` is weakly associated to `M`. The quotient
`R ⧸ I` is auto-associated, and the base change `(R ⧸ I) ⊗[R] N` is projective over it, so by
Stacks 05GP the map `z ↦ (g₁z, …, gₙz)` on that base change — which is not injective after a
further base change to the residue field, by the third hypothesis — is not injective. A nonzero
element `c` of its kernel has an annihilator in `S` containing every `gᵢ` and the image of `I`,
hence contained in no prime missing `𝔮`; any prime minimal over that annihilator is therefore a
prime containing `𝔮` and weakly associated to `N ⊗[R] (R ⧸ I)`. Finally `R ⧸ I` is the submodule
of `M` generated by `y`, and `N` is flat over `R`, so `N ⊗[R] (R ⧸ I)` embeds `S`-linearly in
`N ⊗[R] M` and the annihilator — hence the weakly associated prime — is unchanged. -/
theorem exists_isWeaklyAssociatedPrime_tensorProduct_of_fibre [IsLocalRing R]
    [Module.Projective R N] (hM : IsWeaklyAssociatedPrime R M (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal R))
    (q : Ideal S) {n : ℕ} (g : Fin n → S)
    (hq : q = (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal R).map (algebraMap R S) ⊔ Ideal.span (Set.range g))
    (z : N) (hz : z ∉ IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal R • (⊤ : Submodule R N))
    (hgz : ∀ i, g i • z ∈ IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal R • (⊤ : Submodule R N)) :
    ∃ s : Ideal S, q ≤ s ∧ s.under R = IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal R ∧
      IsWeaklyAssociatedPrime S (N ⊗[R] M) s := by
  classical
  set 𝔭 : Ideal R := IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal R with h𝔭
  -- Step 1: an element of `M` whose annihilator has radical `𝔭`.
  obtain ⟨y, hy⟩ : ∃ y : M, ((R ∙ y).annihilator).radical = 𝔭 :=
    weaklyAssociated_maximalIdeal_iff_exists_radical_eq.mp hM
  set I : Ideal R := (R ∙ y).annihilator with hI
  set A : Type u := R ⧸ I with hA
  have hauto : IsAutoAssociated A :=
    Stacks.AutoAssociated.isAutoAssociated_quotient_of_radical_eq_maximalIdeal hy
  have : Module.Projective A (A ⊗[R] N) := Module.Projective.tensorProduct
  have : Module.Projective A (Fin n → A ⊗[R] N) :=
    Module.Projective.of_equiv'
      (DirectSum.linearEquivFunOnFintype A (Fin n) fun _ => A ⊗[R] N)
  -- Step 2: the map `z ↦ (g₁ z, …, gₙ z)` on `A ⊗[R] N`.
  set Ψ : (A ⊗[R] N) →ₗ[A] (Fin n → A ⊗[R] N) :=
    LinearMap.pi fun i => LinearMap.baseChange A ((LinearMap.lsmul S N (g i)).restrictScalars R)
    with hΨ
  -- Step 3: `Ψ` is not injective after base change to the residue field `R ⧸ 𝔭`.
  have hIle : I ≤ 𝔭 := hy ▸ Ideal.le_radical
  let _ : Algebra A (R ⧸ 𝔭) := (Ideal.Quotient.factor hIle).toAlgebra
  have : IsScalarTower R A (R ⧸ 𝔭) :=
    IsScalarTower.of_algebraMap_eq' (by ext a; exact (Ideal.Quotient.factor_mk hIle a).symm)
  set E : (R ⧸ 𝔭) ⊗[A] (A ⊗[R] N) ≃ₗ[R] N ⧸ 𝔭 • (⊤ : Submodule R N) :=
    (TensorProduct.AlgebraTensorModule.cancelBaseChange R A A (R ⧸ 𝔭) N).restrictScalars R ≪≫ₗ
      TensorProduct.quotTensorEquivQuotSMul N 𝔭 with hE
  have hE1 : ∀ x : N, E (1 ⊗ₜ[A] ((1 : A) ⊗ₜ[R] x)) = Submodule.Quotient.mk x := by
    intro x
    simp [hE, TensorProduct.quotTensorEquivQuotSMul_mk_one_tmul]
  set θ : ((Fin n → A ⊗[R] N) ⊗[A] (R ⧸ 𝔭)) ≃ₗ[A]
      (Fin n → (R ⧸ 𝔭) ⊗[A] (A ⊗[R] N)) :=
    TensorProduct.comm A _ _ ≪≫ₗ TensorProduct.piRight A A (R ⧸ 𝔭) _ with hθ
  have hnotinj : ¬ Function.Injective (Ψ.rTensor (R ⧸ 𝔭)) := by
    intro hinj
    refine hz ?_
    have hker : Ψ.rTensor (R ⧸ 𝔭) (((1 : A) ⊗ₜ[R] z) ⊗ₜ[A] (1 : R ⧸ 𝔭)) = 0 := by
      refine (LinearEquiv.map_eq_zero_iff θ).mp ?_
      funext i
      simp only [Pi.zero_apply]
      rw [show θ (Ψ.rTensor (R ⧸ 𝔭) (((1 : A) ⊗ₜ[R] z) ⊗ₜ[A] (1 : R ⧸ 𝔭))) i
          = (1 : R ⧸ 𝔭) ⊗ₜ[A] ((1 : A) ⊗ₜ[R] (g i • z)) by simp [hθ, hΨ]]
      refine (LinearEquiv.map_eq_zero_iff E).mp ?_
      rw [hE1, Submodule.Quotient.mk_eq_zero]
      exact hgz i
    have h0 : Ψ.rTensor (R ⧸ 𝔭) (0 : (A ⊗[R] N) ⊗[A] (R ⧸ 𝔭)) = 0 := map_zero _
    have h2 : ((1 : A) ⊗ₜ[R] z) ⊗ₜ[A] (1 : R ⧸ 𝔭) = 0 := hinj (hker.trans h0.symm)
    have hEz : E (1 ⊗ₜ[A] ((1 : A) ⊗ₜ[R] z)) = 0 := by
      simpa using congrArg (fun x => E (TensorProduct.comm A (A ⊗[R] N) (R ⧸ 𝔭) x)) h2
    rwa [hE1, Submodule.Quotient.mk_eq_zero] at hEz
  -- Step 4: so `Ψ` itself is not injective.
  have hΨnot : ¬ Function.Injective Ψ :=
    Stacks.AutoAssociated.not_injective_of_not_injective_rTensor hauto Ψ hnotinj
  obtain ⟨a, b, hab, hne⟩ := Function.not_injective_iff.mp hΨnot
  set c₀ : A ⊗[R] N := a - b with hc₀
  have hc₀ne : c₀ ≠ 0 := sub_ne_zero_of_ne hne
  have hc₀ker : ∀ i, LinearMap.baseChange A
      ((LinearMap.lsmul S N (g i)).restrictScalars R) c₀ = 0 := by
    intro i
    have h := congrFun hab i
    simp only [hΨ, LinearMap.pi_apply] at h
    simp [hc₀, map_sub, h]
  -- Step 5: move to `N ⊗[R] A`, where `S` acts.
  set e : (A ⊗[R] N) ≃ₗ[R] (N ⊗[R] A) := TensorProduct.comm R A N with he
  set c : N ⊗[R] A := e c₀ with hc
  have hcne : c ≠ 0 := fun h => hc₀ne (by simpa [hc] using congrArg e.symm h)
  have hcomm : ∀ (i : Fin n) (x : A ⊗[R] N),
      e (LinearMap.baseChange A ((LinearMap.lsmul S N (g i)).restrictScalars R) x)
        = ((LinearMap.lsmul S N (g i)).restrictScalars R).rTensor A (e x) := by
    intro i x
    induction x with
    | zero => simp
    | tmul b m => simp [he]
    | add x y hx hy => simp [hx, hy]
  have hcg : ∀ i, g i • c = 0 := by
    intro i
    rw [show g i • c = ((LinearMap.lsmul S N (g i)).restrictScalars R).rTensor A c from
          TensorProduct.AlgebraTensorModule.smul_eq_lsmul_rTensor (g i) c,
      hc, ← hcomm i c₀, hc₀ker i, map_zero]
  -- Step 6: the annihilator of `c` and a prime minimal over it.
  set J : Ideal S := (S ∙ c).annihilator with hJ
  have hgJ : ∀ i, g i ∈ J := fun i =>
    (Submodule.mem_annihilator_span_singleton c (g i)).mpr (hcg i)
  have hIJ : ∀ a ∈ I, algebraMap R S a ∈ J := fun a ha =>
    (Submodule.mem_annihilator_span_singleton c _).mpr (smul_eq_zero_of_mem I ha c)
  have hJne : J ≠ ⊤ := by
    intro h
    have h1 : (1 : S) ∈ J := h.symm ▸ Submodule.mem_top
    exact hcne (by
      simpa using (Submodule.mem_annihilator_span_singleton c 1).mp h1)
  have hqrad : q ≤ J.radical := by
    rw [hq]
    refine sup_le ?_ ?_
    · rw [Ideal.map_le_iff_le_comap]
      intro a ha
      rw [← hy] at ha
      obtain ⟨k, hk⟩ := ha
      exact ⟨k, by simpa [map_pow] using hIJ _ hk⟩
    · rw [Ideal.span_le]
      rintro _ ⟨i, rfl⟩
      exact Ideal.le_radical (hgJ i)
  obtain ⟨s, hs⟩ := Ideal.nonempty_minimalPrimes hJne
  have hqs : q ≤ s := hqrad.trans ((Ideal.radical_mono hs.1.2).trans_eq hs.1.1.radical)
  refine ⟨s, hqs, ?_, ?_⟩
  -- `s` contains `𝔭S`, so it lies over an ideal of `R` containing the maximal ideal `𝔭`; and it
  -- lies over a proper ideal because it is prime.
  · refine ((IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal.isMaximal R).eq_of_le ?_ ?_).symm
    · intro htop
      refine hs.1.1.ne_top (Ideal.eq_top_of_isUnit_mem s ?_ isUnit_one)
      have h1 : (1 : R) ∈ s.under R := htop.symm ▸ Submodule.mem_top
      simpa using h1
    · intro a ha
      refine hqs ?_
      rw [hq]
      exact Ideal.mem_sup_left (Ideal.mem_map_of_mem _ ha)
  -- Step 7: transport along the `S`-linear embedding `N ⊗[R] A ↪ N ⊗[R] M`.
  · set j : A →ₗ[R] M := I.liftQ (LinearMap.toSpanSingleton R M y) (by
      intro a ha
      simpa [LinearMap.toSpanSingleton_apply] using
        (Submodule.mem_annihilator_span_singleton y a).mp ha) with hj
    have hjinj : Function.Injective j := by
      rw [← LinearMap.ker_eq_bot, hj, Submodule.ker_liftQ_eq_bot]
      · exact le_of_eq (by
          ext a
          simp [LinearMap.toSpanSingleton_apply, hI])
    set ι : (N ⊗[R] A) →ₗ[S] (N ⊗[R] M) :=
      TensorProduct.AlgebraTensorModule.lTensor S N j with hι
    have hιinj : Function.Injective ι := by
      have h : Function.Injective (LinearMap.lTensor N j) :=
        Module.Flat.lTensor_preserves_injective_linearMap j hjinj
      intro x₁ x₂ hx
      refine h ?_
      exact hx
    refine ⟨ι c, ?_⟩
    have hann : (S ∙ (ι c)).annihilator = J := by
      ext b
      rw [Submodule.mem_annihilator_span_singleton, hJ,
        Submodule.mem_annihilator_span_singleton]
      constructor
      · intro h
        refine hιinj ?_
        rw [map_zero, ← h, map_smul]
      · intro h
        rw [← map_smul, h, map_zero]
    rw [hann]
    exact hs

end Stacks.WeaklyAssociatedPrimes

end
